  "facts": [
    "John Frost Bridge, inaugurated after World War II, bears the name of Major‑General John Dutton Frost, who led the 1st Airborne Division’s daring defense of the bridge during Operation Market Garden in 1944.",
    "During the Battle of Arnhem, a flame‑thrower attack on 17 September accidentally ignited ammunition, lighting the bridge’s towers for most of the night and forcing the British to abandon their assault.",
    "On 7 October 1944, U.S. B‑26 Marauders bombed the bridge to deny German reinforcements, yet it survived the war and was rebuilt in 1948, later renamed John Frostbrug in December 1977."
